---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Search Markdown Notes with SQLite FTS5 — Live Demo"
  description="Try SQLite full-text search in your browser. Search sample notes or import Markdown files locally, then explore a reproducible 1k–100k-note benchmark."
  currentPath="/tools/notes-search"
  analytics={false}
  jsonLd={breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Notes search lab', path: '/tools/notes-search' },
  ])}
>
  <section class="content-section lab-page">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <p class="page-kicker">A small working experiment</p>
      <h1>Find the note you remember.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        SQLite full-text search, running in your browser. Start with six sample notes, or bring a
        small folder of your own.
      </p>
      <div id="search-lab" class="lab">
        <div class="lab-top">
          <span>Notes search lab</span><span id="note-count">Six sample notes ready</span>
        </div>
        <button id="start-lab" class="primary">Start search</button>
        <noscript
          ><p>
            Enable JavaScript to run the search demo. The <a
              href="/blog/sqlite-fts5-notes-search-benchmark">tutorial and benchmark</a
            > work without it.
          </p></noscript
        >
        <fieldset disabled>
          <legend class="sr-only">Search controls</legend>
          <form>
            <label for="note-query">What are you looking for?</label>
            <div class="query-row">
              <input
                id="note-query"
                type="search"
                value="sqlite"
                maxlength="200"
                autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="Try sqlite or release checklist"
              /><button type="submit" class="primary">Search</button>
            </div>
            <label class="phrase"><input type="checkbox" id="phrase" /> Match an exact phrase</label
            >
          </form>
          <div class="examples">
            <span>Try:</span><button data-query="sqlite">sqlite</button><button
              data-query="release checklist">release checklist</button
            ><button data-query="backup">backup</button>
          </div>
          <details class="import">
            <summary>Search your own files</summary><p>
              Choose up to 100 Markdown or text files, 2 MB total. They replace the samples. Files
              are read in this tab, not uploaded by the demo. Closing or refreshing the page clears
              the index; your originals are untouched.
            </p><label for="note-files">Choose .md or .txt files</label><input
              id="note-files"
              type="file"
              multiple
              accept=".md,.txt"
            /><button id="reset-notes" type="button">Restore sample notes</button>
          </details>
        </fieldset>
        <p id="lab-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">
          Start to load the SQLite engine. No account needed.
        </p>
        <ol id="lab-results" aria-label="Search results"></ol>
      </div>
      <div class="post-content">
        <h2>Small enough to understand</h2>
        <p>
          This uses SQLite FTS5 in a web worker, with an in-memory index and ranked results. All
          words must match unless you choose exact phrase. It searches word tokens, not arbitrary
          substrings or semantic similarity. Markdown is indexed as plain text, including its
          markup.
        </p>
        <p>
          The timer measures the count and ranked-result queries inside the worker. It excludes
          engine download, indexing, messaging, and rendering. It is not directly comparable with
          the native Python benchmark.
        </p>
        <p>
          Note text, filenames, and searches are not sent to a server by this demo. PostHog is
          disabled on this page. Hosting may still collect ordinary page-visit analytics.
        </p>
        <h2>Measure it yourself</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="/blog/sqlite-fts5-notes-search-benchmark"
            >Read the SQLite notes-search tutorial and 1k–100k-note benchmark</a
          >, including the schema, limitations, raw timings, and a script you can run locally.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a larger application, see <a href="/blog/markdown-notes-sqlite-search-index"
            >how Stone combines full-text search and embeddings</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<script>
  import '../../components/search-lab/client';
</script>
<style>
  .lab-page h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display, 'Newsreader', serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.06;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .lab {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 20%, transparent);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .lab-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  #note-count,
  #lab-status {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  fieldset {
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  fieldset:disabled {
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .query-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  input[type='search'] {
    min-width: 0;
    flex: 1;
    padding: 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    font: inherit;
  }
  button {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 25%, transparent);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: scale 120ms;
  }
  button:active {
    scale: 0.96;
  }
  button.primary {
    background: var(--fg);
    color: var(--bg);
  }
  #start-lab {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  :where(button, input, summary):focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .phrase {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    min-height: 44px;
    margin: 0.5rem 0;
  }
  .phrase input {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
  }
  .examples {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .import {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    min-height: 44px;
    align-content: center;
  }
  .import p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  input[type='file'] {
    max-width: 100%;
    display: block;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  #lab-status {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  #lab-results {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  #lab-results :global(li) {
    padding: 1.2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, currentColor 15%, transparent);
    margin-top: 1rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  #lab-results :global(h3) {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  #lab-results :global(p) {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .lab {
      padding: 1rem;
    }
    .query-row {
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .query-row input {
      flex-basis: 100%;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    button {
      transition: none;
    }
    button:active {
      scale: 1;
    }
  }
</style>
